<title>USA: Merck to buy back $5 billion of its stock.</title>
<headline>Merck to buy back $5 billion of its stock.</headline>
<dateline>WHITEHOUSE STATION, N.J.</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merck &amp; Co. Inc. said Tuesday it will buy back $5 billion more of its stock, in addition to a $3 billion buyback underway, but the news failed to impress investors and the drug maker's stock fell.</p>
<p>The Whitehouse Station, N.J.-based company said the stock, to be acquired on the open market and in private transactions, would be used for employee benefit programmes or for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Merck stock fell 62.5 cents to $97.75 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
